    <section class="section" id="consequence">
      <h2><span class="num">05 — Consequence</span>First Instance</h2>
      <p>The enforcement terms are specific. Up to €250,000 per violation in contempt penalties (<em lang="de">Ordnungsgeld</em>). Security deposits of €150,000 per injunction provision, €70,000 for accounting and damages claims, €10,000 for the publication order. Pre-litigation attorney fees of €5,049.70. Suno was represented by Latham &amp; Watkins.</p>

      <p>Suno responded on the day of the ruling: "We disagree with today's ruling — which rests on a fundamental mischaracterization of how Suno's technology works, how it is used and how US law applies — and are evaluating all available options, including an appeal." The company has separately stated that it "built protections into our platform" and trained its models "to create new songs, not reproduce existing ones."</p>

      <p>The judgment is first instance and not final. As of 18 August 2026, Suno has not confirmed filing an appeal. Under German procedure, the <em lang="de">Berufung</em> deadline runs from service of the fully reasoned judgment, which has not been publicly released. An appeal would go to the Oberlandesgericht München — the same court currently hearing the GEMA v. OpenAI appeal, for which no hearing date has been publicly established. The fully reasoned judgment (<em lang="de">Urteilsbegründung</em>) has not been made available in standard legal databases. The most detailed public analysis, by Tobias Vossberg at itmr-legal, appears to have accessed an officially released version of the judgment, but the text is not freely accessible for independent reader verification.</p>

      <p>Two pending proceedings could alter the landscape. The CJEU preliminary reference in <em>Like Company v. Google</em> (C-250/25) — the first CJEU case on generative AI and copyright — held its first oral hearing on 10 March 2026. An Advocate General opinion is expected around September 2026. Either that case or the OpenAI appeal could reshape the legal framework before any Suno appeal is heard.</p>

      <p>Eight days before the verdict, on 23 July 2026, GEMA launched PLAI by GEMA — described as Europe's first fully licensed AI music training dataset, comprising approximately 178,000 sound files across more than 60 genres with copyright and master rights clearances. GEMA is positioning itself simultaneously as enforcer and licensor. The International Federation of the Phonographic Industry stated: "This landmark decision by the Munich Court reinforces the principle that the use of music to develop commercial AI products requires authorisation from right holders."</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="signal">
      <h2><span class="num">06 — Signal</span>The Jurisdictional Fracture</h2>
      <p>The ruling instantiates a structural pattern. A collecting society used its domestic venue rule to reach training conducted in a foreign country. The court asserted jurisdiction, applied that foreign country's own copyright law, and found infringement. The mechanism is replicable. Any collecting society in any jurisdiction with analogous venue rules can attempt the same.</p>

      <p>There is concrete evidence the pattern is already spreading. The Danish collecting society Koda sued Suno in November 2025 over stream-ripping and unauthorised training. GEMA v. OpenAI, decided at first instance and now on appeal, extends the same logic to a different defendant. GEMA CEO Tobias Holzmüller stated on the day of the Suno ruling: <span lang="de">"Menschliche Kreativität ist die Grundlage jeder generativen KI"</span> — human creativity is the foundation of all generative AI.</p>

      <p>The UK law firm Bristows, in its analysis of the decision, concluded that "offshoring training will not insulate against German collecting society claims" and identified memorisation as "a live commercial risk." The practical position, Bristows noted, remains unsettled pending the OpenAI appeal, CJEU guidance, and a potential Suno appeal. But the structural question this ruling surfaces does not depend on any single appeal. A model is one artifact — a single set of weights. It faces every court that can reach it. Each court applies its own choice-of-law rules to select potentially different national laws. Each court is correct within its own legal framework. The question is whether compliance with all of them simultaneously is possible, when you cannot selectively un-memorise one jurisdiction's repertoire from a set of weights without retraining the entire model.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</StoryLayout>

<script>
(function () {
  const canvas = document.querySelector('.gema-suno-training-ruling-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
  if (!canvas) return;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  if (!ctx) return;

  /* colours from CSS */
  const cs = getComputedStyle(canvas);
  const bgHex = cs.getPropertyValue('--bg').trim() || '#0d0d0d';
  const storyHex = cs.getPropertyValue('--story').trim() || '#d4764e';

  function hexRgb(hex: string): [number, number, number] {
    const h = hex.replace('#', '');
    if (!/^[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/.test(h)) return [212, 118, 78];
    return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];
  }
  const [sR, sG, sB] = hexRgb(storyHex);
  const DR = 232, DG = 232, DB = 232;

  /* timing constants */
  const MAX      = 70;
  const FALL_VY  = 0.3;
  const SPAWN_IV = 3;
  const P_CALM   = 720;
  const P_GRAV   = 840;
  const P_HOLD   = 880;
  const CYCLE    = 900;

  /* mutable state */
  let W = 0, H = 0, rafId = 0, frame = 0, spawnClk = 0;
  let lR = 50;
  let llx = 0, lly = 0;
  let rlx = 0, rly = 0;
  let absorbN = 0, glowA = 0;
  const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  interface Pt {
    x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number;
    a: number; r: number; st: number;
    mix: number; orbA: number; orbR: number;
    rDir: number; ent: number;
  }

  const pts: Pt[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < MAX; i++) {
    pts.push({ x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, a: 0, r: 0, st: 0,
               mix: 0, orbA: 0, orbR: 0, rDir: 0, ent: 0 });
  }

  function emit(p: Pt, y0?: number) {
    p.x   = Math.random() * W;
    p.y   = y0 !== undefined ? y0 : (-2 - Math.random() * 12);
    p.vx  = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.1;
    p.vy  = FALL_VY * (0.88 + Math.random() * 0.24);
    p.a   = 0.09 + Math.random() * 0.15;
    p.r   = 1.2 + Math.random() * 0.8;
    p.st  = 1;
    p.mix = 0;
    p.orbA = Math.random() * 6.2832;
    p.orbR = 0;
    p.rDir = 0;
    p.ent  = 0;
  }

  function lensPos() {
    lR  = Math.min(W, H) * 0.14;
    llx = W * 0.30;  lly = H * 0.40;
    rlx = W * 0.70;  rly = H * 0.40;
  }

  function seed() {
    const n = Math.min(18, MAX);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) emit(pts[i], Math.random() * H * 0.30);
  }

  function resetCycle() {
    frame = 0; spawnClk = 0; absorbN = 0; glowA = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < MAX; i++) pts[i].st = 0;
    seed();
  }

  function update() {
    const cf = frame % CYCLE;
    lensPos();
    const lR2 = lR * lR;

    const isCalm  = cf < P_CALM;
    const isGrav  = cf >= P_CALM && cf < P_GRAV;
    const isHold  = cf >= P_GRAV && cf < P_HOLD;
    const isReset = cf >= P_HOLD;

    if (isCalm || isGrav) {
      if (++spawnClk >= SPAWN_IV) {
        spawnClk = 0;
        for (let j = 0; j < MAX; j++) {
          if (pts[j].st === 0) { emit(pts[j]); break; }
        }
      }
    }

    const gS = isGrav ? ((cf - P_CALM) / (P_GRAV - P_CALM)) * 0.02
             : isHold ? 0.02 : 0;

    for (let i = 0; i < MAX; i++) {
      const p = pts[i];
      if (p.st === 0) continue;

      if (p.st === 1) {
        p.vx += Math.sin(p.y * 0.014 + i * 2.1 + frame * 0.007) * 0.002;
        if (p.vx >  0.3) p.vx =  0.3;
        if (p.vx < -0.3) p.vx = -0.3;

        if (gS > 0) {
          const dx = rlx - p.x, dy = rly - p.y;
          const d  = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
          if (d > 5) {
            const pull = gS * Math.min(1.0, 140 / d);
            p.vx += (dx / d) * pull;
            p.vy += (dy / d) * pull * 0.3;
          }
        }

        p.x += p.vx;
        p.y += p.vy;

        if ((frame - p.ent) > 60) {
          const dxL = p.x - llx, dyL = p.y - lly;
          if (dxL * dxL + dyL * dyL < lR2 && p.y < lly) {
            p.st = 2; p.ent = frame;
            p.rDir = dxL < 0 ? -1 : dxL > 0 ? 1 : (Math.random() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1);
          }
        }

        const dxR = p.x - rlx, dyR = p.y - rly;
        if (dxR * dxR + dyR * dyR < lR2) {
          p.st = 3; p.ent = frame;
        }

        if (p.y > H + 15 || p.x < -25 || p.x > W + 25) p.st = 0;

      } else if (p.st === 2) {
        const el = frame - p.ent;
        if (el < 25) {
          p.vy = 0.15 + el * 0.002;
          p.vx += p.rDir * 0.006;
          if (p.vx >  0.4) p.vx =  0.4;
          if (p.vx < -0.4) p.vx = -0.4;
          if (gS > 0) {
            const dxG = rlx - p.x, dyG = rly - p.y;
            const dG  = Math.sqrt(dxG * dxG + dyG * dyG);
            if (dG > 5) p.vx += (dxG / dG) * gS * Math.min(1, 140 / dG) * 0.5;
          }
        } else {
          p.st = 1;
          p.vy = FALL_VY;
        }
        p.x += p.vx;
        p.y += p.vy;
        if (p.y > H + 15 || el > 200) p.st = 0;

      } else if (p.st === 3) {
        const el3 = frame - p.ent;
        p.vx *= 0.94;
        p.vy *= 0.94;
        const dxA = rlx - p.x, dyA = rly - p.y;
        const dA  = Math.sqrt(dxA * dxA + dyA * dyA);
        if (dA > 2) {
          p.vx += (dxA / dA) * 0.018;
          p.vy += (dyA / dA) * 0.018;
        }
        p.x += p.vx;
        p.y += p.vy;
        p.mix = Math.min(1, el3 / 30);
        p.r   = Math.max(0.5, p.r - 0.008);
        if (el3 > 40) {
          p.st   = 4;
          p.orbA = Math.atan2(p.y - rly, p.x - rlx);
          p.orbR = lR * (0.45 + Math.random() * 0.42);
          absorbN++;
          glowA = Math.min(0.35, absorbN * 0.01);
        }

      } else if (p.st === 4) {
        p.orbA += 0.002;
        p.x   = rlx + Math.cos(p.orbA) * p.orbR;
        p.y   = rly + Math.sin(p.orbA) * p.orbR;
        p.mix = 1;
        p.a   = Math.max(0.02, p.a - 0.0003);
        p.r   = Math.max(0.3, p.r - 0.0004);
      }
    }

    if (isReset) {
      glowA *= 0.82;
      for (let k = 0; k < MAX; k++) {
        if (pts[k].st > 0) {
          pts[k].a *= 0.82;
          if (pts[k].a < 0.003) pts[k].st = 0;
        }
      }
    }

    if (cf >= CYCLE - 1) resetCycle();
  }

  function rings(cx: number, cy: number, r: number, alpha: number) {
    ctx!.lineWidth = 1;
    for (let k = 0; k < 3; k++) {
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(cx, cy, r * (0.50 + k * 0.25), 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.strokeStyle = 'rgba(' + DR + ',' + DG + ',' + DB + ',' + alpha + ')';
      ctx!.stroke();
    }
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgHex;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    rings(llx, lly, lR, 0.06);
    rings(rlx, rly, lR, 0.06 + glowA * 0.5);

    if (glowA > 0.003) {
      const gr = ctx!.createRadialGradient(rlx, rly, 0, rlx, rly, lR * 1.05);
      gr.addColorStop(0,    'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',' + glowA + ')');
      gr.addColorStop(0.55, 'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',' + (glowA * 0.35) + ')');
      gr.addColorStop(1,    'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',0)');
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(rlx, rly, lR * 1.05, 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.fillStyle = gr;
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    const cf = frame % CYCLE;
    if (cf >= P_CALM && cf < P_HOLD) {
      const gp = cf < P_GRAV ? (cf - P_CALM) / (P_GRAV - P_CALM) : 1;
      const fR = lR * (1.3 + gp * 2.5);
      const fA = gp * 0.035;
      if (fA > 0.002) {
        const gf = ctx!.createRadialGradient(rlx, rly, lR, rlx, rly, fR);
        gf.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',' + fA + ')');
        gf.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',0)');
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(rlx, rly, fR, 0, 6.2832);
        ctx!.fillStyle = gf;
        ctx!.fill();
      }
    }

    for (let i = 0; i < MAX; i++) {
      const p = pts[i];
      if (p.st === 0 || p.a < 0.003) continue;
      const cr = (DR + (sR - DR) * p.mix) | 0;
      const cg = (DG + (sG - DG) * p.mix) | 0;
      const cb = (DB + (sB - DB) * p.mix) | 0;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(p.x, p.y, Math.max(0.3, p.r), 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.fillStyle = 'rgba(' + cr + ',' + cg + ',' + cb + ',' + p.a + ')';
      ctx!.fill();
    }
  }

  function drawStatic() {
    lensPos();
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgHex;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    rings(llx, lly, lR, 0.06);
    rings(rlx, rly, lR, 0.13);

    const gr = ctx!.createRadialGradient(rlx, rly, 0, rlx, rly, lR);
    gr.addColorStop(0,   'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',0.12)');
    gr.addColorStop(0.6, 'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',0.04)');
    gr.addColorStop(1,   'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',0)');
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(rlx, rly, lR, 0, 6.2832);
    ctx!.fillStyle = gr;
    ctx!.fill();

    for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
      const px = (i / 20) * W + Math.sin(i * 4.3) * 10;
      const py = H * 0.06 + Math.sin(i * 2.7) * H * 0.25 + H * 0.12;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(px, py, 1.2, 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.fillStyle = 'rgba(' + DR + ',' + DG + ',' + DB + ',0.09)';
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    for (let j = 0; j < 4; j++) {
      const ry = lly - lR * 0.35 + j * lR * 0.22;
      const rx = llx + (j - 1.5) * 7;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(rx, ry, 1.1, 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.fillStyle = 'rgba(' + DR + ',' + DG + ',' + DB + ',0.10)';
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    for (let j2 = 0; j2 < 3; j2++) {
      const ty = lly + lR * 0.3 + j2 * lR * 0.28;
      const tx = llx + (j2 + 1) * 9;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(tx, ty, 1.1, 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.fillStyle = 'rgba(' + DR + ',' + DG + ',' + DB + ',0.07)';
      ctx!.fill();
    }

    for (let k = 0; k < 7; k++) {
      const ang = (k / 7) * 6.2832;
      const oR  = lR * (0.50 + (k % 3) * 0.15);
      const ox  = rlx + Math.cos(ang) * oR;
      const oy  = rly + Math.sin(ang) * oR;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(ox, oy, 0.9, 0, 6.2832);
      ctx!.fillStyle = 'rgba(' + sR + ',' + sG + ',' + sB + ',0.14)';
      ctx!.fill();
    }
  }

  function tick() {
    frame++;
    update();
    draw();
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }

  function resize() {
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    W = canvas!.offsetWidth;
    H = canvas!.offsetHeight;
    canvas!.width  = Math.round(W * dpr);
    canvas!.height = Math.round(H * dpr);
    ctx!.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    lensPos();
    if (reduced) drawStatic();
  }

  const ro = new ResizeObserver(resize);
  ro.observe(canvas);

  resize();

  if (reduced) {
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', function () { ro.disconnect(); });
  } else {
    seed();
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      if (entries[0].isIntersecting) {
        if (!rafId) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
      } else {
        cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
        rafId = 0;
      }
    }, { threshold: 0.01 });
    io.observe(canvas);
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', function () {
      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
      rafId = 0;
      io.disconnect();
      ro.disconnect();
    });
  }
})();
</script>
